1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,085
Athens, 1963.

2
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:10,554
A blood culture from a patient named Temoneira grows E. coli that should have died on penicillin.

3
00:00:10,604 --> 00:00:11,514
It did not.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,280
The enzyme that saved it got her name.

5
00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:20,718
TEM. You met it in episode one: it waits in the periplasm and breaks the drug before it reaches the wall.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,767
So where does it come from?

7
00:00:22,817 --> 00:00:23,937
Not from the chromosome.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:25,757
From this.

9
00:00:25,807 --> 00:00:33,181
A plasmid: a spare ring of DNA, a few thousand base pairs, with one gene on it that matters.

10
00:00:33,231 --> 00:00:34,149
A passenger.

11
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:35,992
The gene is read.

12
00:00:36,042 --> 00:00:37,453
The protein is made.

13
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:45,915
A signal sequence at its front sends it across the inner membrane, into the periplasm, to wait by the door.

14
00:00:45,965 --> 00:00:49,326
One ring of DNA, and the whole cell is covered.

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,210
Now the part that should worry you.

16
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,372
Bacteria have sex.

17
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:00,396
A pilus, the sex pilus, hooks a neighbour that has no enzyme, and pulls it close.

18
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,825
One strand of the ring crosses.

19
00:01:02,875 --> 00:01:06,453
The neighbour builds the other strand and closes the circle.

20
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,016
It did not evolve resistance.

21
00:01:10,066 --> 00:01:11,227
It was handed it.

22
00:01:11,277 --> 00:01:12,011
In minutes.

23
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,817
The gene is read there too.

24
00:01:14,867 --> 00:01:17,513
The enzyme is shipped to the periplasm.

25
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:19,818
Same drug.

26
00:01:19,868 --> 00:01:20,686
Same door.

27
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:23,833
Ring broken.

28
00:01:23,883 --> 00:01:25,305
The cell carries on.

29
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:36,310
Within ten years of Athens, the same gene was in gonorrhoea, and in the Haemophilus that gives children meningitis.

30
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,619
Different species.

31
00:01:37,669 --> 00:01:38,709
Same passenger.

32
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,410
A plasmid can cross in minutes.

33
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:44,472
A ward can turn in a week.

34
00:01:44,522 --> 00:01:51,930
A gene found in one species, in one country, is a problem for every species, in every country.

35
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,019
Resistance does not need a stronger cell.

36
00:01:56,069 --> 00:01:58,190
It needs a gene that travels.

